╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_tree_broadcast                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The original implementation uses one independent Dijkstra shortest path per destination   │
│                          │ and copies that identical route to every partition. Its main parameters are the edge      │
│                          │ `cost` weight, `num_partitions`, and the implicit single-path selection criterion. It     │
│                          │ does not account for overlapping destination routes, shared transfer trunks, unavailable  │
│                          │ costs, or link throughput.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version keeps the same function inputs and `BroadCastTopology` output, but improves  │
│                          │ routing with a cost-aware directed broadcast-tree heuristic. It first computes individual │
│                          │ shortest paths as a safe baseline, then builds several shared multicast-tree candidates   │
│                          │ using adaptive marginal edge cost: edges already present in the broadcast tree have zero  │
│                          │ additional cost, encouraging destinations to reuse paid transfer trunks and branch only   │
│                          │ when needed. Candidate trees are compared using shared-edge cost first and total route    │
│                          │ cost second. The selected tree is only accepted when its per-destination route cost       │
│                          │ remains within a small adaptive stretch threshold (`MAX_ROUTE_STRETCH = 0.02`) of         │
│                          │ independent shortest paths. All partitions are emitted on the selected low-cost route,    │
│                          │ allowing partitions to be transferred concurrently while retaining overlapping shared     │
│                          │ paths.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key configuration choices:                                                                │
│                          │ - `MAX_ROUTE_STRETCH = 0.02`: permits at most 2% additional individual path cost when it  │
│                          │ substantially reduces shared broadcast cost.                                              │
│                          │ - `TREE_SEEDS = 4`: tests several destination orderings to avoid greedy-order bias.       │
│                          │ - `SHARED_EDGE_WEIGHT = 0.0`: previously selected tree edges have zero marginal broadcast │
│                          │ cost.                                                                                     │
│                          │ - Throughput is preserved in edge metadata and used as a deterministic tie-breaker,       │
│                          │ preferring higher-bandwidth equivalent-cost paths.                                        │
