│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_multicast_tree                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace independent per-destination shortest paths with a greedy directed multicast-tree  │
│                          │ construction. The previous implementation optimizes each destination in isolation,        │
│                          │ repeatedly paying for identical source-side links. This edit grows one low-cost broadcast │
│                          │ tree: at each step it attaches the destination that can be reached most cheaply from any  │
│                          │ node already in the tree. Routes are then derived from the shared tree for every          │
│                          │ destination and reused by every partition.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a practical directed-Steiner-tree heuristic. It preserves valid                   │
│                          │ source-to-destination paths while reducing duplicate inter-cloud transfers, especially    │
│                          │ when multiple destinations share regional transit links. Invalid or unpriced links are    │
│                          │ excluded, preventing routes from being selected through edges that cannot contribute to a │
│                          │ meaningful transfer-cost calculation.                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0225                                                                                   │
