│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exact_shared_broadcast                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the locally greedy tree growth with an exact directed-Steiner dynamic program for │
│                          │ normal-sized destination sets. The current greedy approach can commit to a cheap early    │
│                          │ branch that prevents a substantially cheaper shared backbone from being selected later.   │
│                          │ The subset dynamic program explicitly minimizes the union cost of all broadcast edges by  │
│                          │ combining destination subsets at shared relay nodes and relaxing those shared subtrees    │
│                          │ backwards through the network.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For larger destination sets, retain a scalable shared-tree fallback, but validate numeric │
│                          │ prices and exclude source-incoming links, self loops, and invalid pricing consistently.   │
│                          │ The resulting topology still uses the existing BroadCastTopology contract and assigns     │
│                          │ every partition the selected shared route, permitting downstream transfer overlap.        │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
