│ patch_name               │ frontier_mergecast                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces independent destination routing with a frontier-based        │
│                          │ multicast construction algorithm. It starts from the source or a seeded low-cost          │
│                          │ destination path, then repeatedly grows a shared directed transfer tree by connecting the │
│                          │ cheapest remaining destination from any node already reached by the broadcast.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The approach is inspired by shortest-path and shared-tree ideas in the context programs,  │
│                          │ but differs by using multi-source frontier expansion rather than recomputing              │
│                          │ source-to-destination paths with zeroed edge costs. This makes tree growth explicit,      │
│                          │ preserves valid parent relationships for every route, and naturally favors reusable       │
│                          │ trunks. Several seeded tree candidates are evaluated, including the unseeded tree and     │
│                          │ trees initialized with individual shortest paths. The selected topology minimizes unique  │
│                          │ broadcast-edge cost first, then total receiver route cost as a tie-breaker. Invalid-cost  │
│                          │ links, source inbound links, self-loops, missing destinations, and disconnected graphs    │
│                          │ are handled safely.                                                                       │
