│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_broadcast_tree                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace independent per-destination shortest paths with a greedy directed broadcast-tree  │
│                          │ construction. The algorithm repeatedly attaches the destination that can be reached with  │
│                          │ the lowest additional network cost from any node already receiving the broadcast. Once an │
│                          │ intermediate node has received data, it becomes a free relay point for subsequent         │
│                          │ destinations, avoiding repeated source-to-relay transfers.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The resulting tree is expanded into the existing per-destination path representation so   │
│                          │ that BroadCastTopology remains compatible. Every partition uses the same low-cost relay   │
│                          │ tree, preserving parallel partition transfers while ensuring that shared prefixes and     │
│                          │ intermediate relays are reused rather than independently recreated for every destination. │
│                          │ Edges without usable costs are excluded before routing, preventing incomplete cost-grid   │
│                          │ entries from being selected.                                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
