│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exact_steiner_broadcast                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the greedy relay-attachment heuristic with an exact dynamic-programming directed  │
│                          │ Steiner arborescence search for manageable destination sets. The existing greedy approach │
│                          │ can commit to an inexpensive early relay branch that prevents a substantially cheaper     │
│                          │ shared backbone from being selected later.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement optimizes the cost of the union of broadcast edges: a dynamic-programming │
│                          │ state represents the minimum-cost subnetwork rooted at every possible relay node for      │
│                          │ every subset of destinations. It combines already solved destination subsets at common    │
│                          │ relay nodes, then propagates those solutions backward through incoming links. This        │
│                          │ identifies shared network segments globally rather than only sharing paths                │
│                          │ opportunistically.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The reconstructed directed subgraph is then converted into complete source-to-destination │
│                          │ paths for `BroadCastTopology`, preserving its existing interface and partition behavior.  │
│                          │ Unpriced edges, self loops, and inbound edges to the source remain excluded so the        │
│                          │ routing objective remains valid.                                                          │
