│ patch_name               │ prune_irrelevant_relays                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Restrict the Steiner dynamic program to relay nodes that can both be reached from the     │
│                          │ source and can reach at least one requested destination. Nodes outside this intersection  │
│                          │ cannot participate in any valid broadcast arborescence, but previously consumed           │
│                          │ state-space, Dijkstra relaxation, and reconstruction work for every destination subset.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This preserves the optimal transfer cost exactly while substantially reducing the         │
│                          │ exponential solver’s effective graph size on multi-cloud topologies containing unrelated  │
│                          │ regions or one-way links. The reduced state space makes it more practical to solve larger │
│                          │ destination sets exactly, rather than spending time evaluating routes that cannot         │
│                          │ contribute to a shared broadcast backbone.                                                │
