│ patch_description        │ Replace the anchor-greedy attachment heuristic with an exact directed Steiner dynamic     │
│                          │ program for practical destination-set sizes. The planner evaluates every possible subset  │
│                          │ merge at every relay, then propagates those shared subtree costs backward over priced     │
│                          │ links. This finds the minimum-cost shared broadcast arborescence rather than committing   │
│                          │ early to locally cheap branches. A bounded fallback preserves scalability for unusually   │
│                          │ large receiver sets while retaining shared-trunk behavior.                                │
