│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exact_steiner_broadcast                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the local cheapest-branch heuristic with an exact directed-Steiner dynamic        │
│                          │ program for modest destination sets. The existing greedy approach can commit to an        │
│                          │ inexpensive early branch that prevents a globally cheaper shared trunk from being         │
│                          │ selected. The new planner minimizes the union cost of directed edges needed to reach      │
│                          │ every receiver, which directly matches broadcast billing where a shared edge is           │
│                          │ transferred once and then fanned out downstream.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The DP uses subset states over destinations and reverse multi-source Dijkstra relaxation  │
│                          │ to efficiently find the least-cost directed arborescence rooted at the source. For        │
│                          │ unusually large terminal sets it retains a deterministic shared-tree greedy fallback,     │
│                          │ avoiding exponential state growth. It also validates costs, handles missing/unreachable   │
│                          │ destinations without exceptions, and explicitly initializes empty paths for unreachable   │
│                          │ receivers.                                                                                │
