│ patch_description        │ Extend exact shared-transfer optimization to moderately larger destination sets by first  │
│                          │ reducing the network to low-slack source-to-terminal corridors. The reduction preserves   │
│                          │ every shortest route while retaining reasonably priced relay alternatives, which are      │
│                          │ where multicast trunks and cross-cloud reuse are most likely to occur. This makes the     │
│                          │ directed-Steiner DP practical for up to 14 destinations instead of falling immediately to │
│                          │ the greedy attachment strategy at 12 destinations.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The reduction is applied only for fan-outs that previously used the greedy fallback, so   │
│                          │ existing exact behavior for smaller configurations is unchanged. A generous per-terminal  │
│                          │ slack retains alternative relay paths while avoiding DP work across unrelated network     │
│                          │ regions.                                                                                  │
