│ patch_description        │ This version improves broadcast planning by combining exact directed-Steiner optimization │
│                          │ for manageable destination groups with DP-guided corridor clustering for larger fan-outs. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Uses exact directed Steiner DP on the full valid network for up to 13 reachable         │
│                          │ destinations, avoiding corridor pruning that can exclude globally optimal shared routes.  │
│                          │ - For larger fan-outs, groups destinations according to overlap in reverse shortest-path  │
│                          │ corridors, then solves each overlapping cluster exactly.                                  │
│                          │ - Produces a union of shared relay edges, reducing redundant source-to-destination        │
│                          │ transfers.                                                                                │
│                          │ - Includes a greedy shared-tree fallback and selects the lowest-cost valid candidate      │
│                          │ topology.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Removes invalid, self-loop, source-return, missing-cost, and negative-cost edges before │
│                          │ optimization.                                                                             │
│                          │ - Preserves the existing `BroadCastTopology`, `search_algorithm`, and `make_nx_graph`     │
│                          │ interfaces and outputs.                                                                   │
