│ patch_name               │ terminal_corridor_reduction                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Add a terminal-aware corridor reduction before the exponential directed-Steiner dynamic   │
│                          │ program. The reduction retains every shortest source-to-terminal corridor plus controlled │
│                          │ near-shortest alternatives, which preserves useful shared relay opportunities while       │
│                          │ removing regions and links that cannot plausibly participate in an economical multicast   │
│                          │ tree. The slack is expanded automatically if the first reduction disconnects a terminal,  │
│                          │ ensuring feasibility is never sacrificed. This reduces DP state work on multi-cloud       │
│                          │ topologies and makes it practical to optimize larger fan-outs while still favoring shared │
│                          │ broadcast trunks over redundant direct transfers.                                         │
