│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ corridor_reduced_steiner_dp                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce the graph to terminal-aware low-cost source-to-destination corridors before        │
│                          │ invoking the exponential directed-Steiner DP, then increase the exact-DP limit from 14 to │
│                          │ 16 terminals.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For fan-outs above 14 destinations, the existing implementation immediately falls back to │
│                          │ greedy attachment, which can miss a low-cost shared trunk. The reduction computes         │
│                          │ shortest source distances and reverse shortest distances from every terminal, retaining   │
│                          │ edges that lie near at least one low-slack source-terminal route. This preserves          │
│                          │ inexpensive relay and backbone opportunities while removing unrelated cloud links from    │
│                          │ the DP state space. With fewer active relay nodes, exact optimization remains practical   │
│                          │ for moderately larger fan-outs and can select shared paths that greedy routing does not   │
│                          │ discover. Individual shortest-path corridors are always retained, so the reduced graph    │
│                          │ still has a feasible route for every reachable destination.                               │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
