│                          │ Destinations whose independently cheapest routes share trunk edges are grouped together,  │
│                          │ then each group is solved with the exact directed Steiner dynamic program. This retains   │
│                          │ scalable runtime while allowing each correlated destination group to discover non-greedy  │
│                          │ shared relays and trunks. The resulting cluster subnetworks are unioned, preserving       │
│                          │ overlap between groups without repeatedly charging or transmitting along redundant        │
│                          │ source-side paths.                                                                        │
